nd hype out of the  present  atmosphere of i would even say hate that  seems to be prevailing in russia  the  hate antagonism specifically between  russia and and ukraine but in a broader  sense and so i very much support this  initiative  and so uh but beyond that for me to  spend an evening talking in russian  eating russian food experiencing that  russian  atmosphere that i i so much enjoy was a  reward and and just a final note  communicating of course includes  speaking but it's not only speaking and  just out of curiosity i looked at my  statistics at link  and i have read about you know one oh  well over a million words in russian  according to my statistics at link so i  have read much more than that uh i think  i have listened  i mean every day just about i download  from echo must be two three or four  interviews each interview is 30 40  minutes long i'm sure i've listened to  six seven thousand hours of russian over  the last nine ten years  but how much have i spoken again mostly  i've spoken with our tutors at link we  keep those statistics i've spoken 150  hours  throw in another 10 or 15 hours where  i've met people like the other evening  and spoken so i have listened 50 times  more than i have spoken that's not  because i don't want to speak i just  haven't had the opportunity whereas  there's ample opportunity to listen and  read  listening and reading is communicating  it's a wonderful way to communicate it  prepares you for those great  opportunities when you can actually talk  and use the language and of course the  more you talk the better you get at  speaking but listening and reading is  also communicating  and that's  kind of the point i wanted to make  tonight and i'm gonna make another video  again on the subject of of communicating  and and and listening and what we should  listen to and what we should read to  make it meaningful so thanks very much  bye for now
 

